From: Paul Durston <paul.durston@durston-scaffolding.example> (Paul Durston Ltd / Durston Scaffolding Ltd)
To: Barry Norfolk <barry.norfolk@rotamead.example> (Rotamead)
Date: 2017-03-31
Subject: Re: Outstanding Debt 31st March 2017

Letter 1, on Paul Durston Limited headed paper, signed by Paul Durston:

Further to our meeting on Tuesday 21st March 2017, we write to confirm that as of 1st April 2017, Paul Durston Limited T/A Scaffolding transfers all hire duties and obligations (as detailed on hire invoice Nr's H29872 and H29873) and the outstanding debt of £186,564.48 to Durston Scaffolding Limited. We trust the above is satisfactory.
Yours sincerely, Paul Durston

Letter 2, on Durston Scaffolding Limited headed paper, signed by Jamie Ryan:

As from 1st April 2017, Durston Scaffolding Limited accepts all hire duties and obligations and agrees the hire material quantities as detailed in hire invoices H29872 and H29873, and accepts the outstanding debt of £186,564.48 from Paul Durston Limited trading as Durston Scaffolding.

--
RECONSTRUCTED FROM THE PUBLISHED JUDGMENT. Not an original document.
Source: Rotamead v Durston Scaffolding [2020] EWHC 2738 (TCC), paras 1 (agreed chronology), 3, 18-20, 53.
The judgment quotes the PDL letter with £186,554.48 and elsewhere gives £186,561.48; the judge treats £186,564.48 as the agreed figure. Letter 2 wording follows Mr Norfolk's 30 March 2017 email requesting it, as its own text is not quoted.
